{"type":"lesson.started","request_id":"9c95f2d5-156e-44aa-bf4f-f983678c64e4","title":"Superposition of two waves: constructive and destructive"}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"9c95f2d5-156e-44aa-bf4f-f983678c64e4","step":{"id":"s1","script":"Superposition means adding displacements at each position. Compare two unit-amplitude waves: aligned on the left, opposite on the right.","ops":[{"op":"figure","id":"construct","region":"left","frame":{"x":[0,6.28],"y":[-2.5,2.9],"axes":"edge","x_label":"position x","y_label":"displacement"},"marks":[{"kind":"fn","id":"wave_a","y":"sin(x)","domain":[0,6.28]},{"kind":"fn","id":"wave_b","y":"sin(x)","domain":[0,6.28],"stroke":"dashed"},{"kind":"text","at":[3.14,2.5],"text":"In phase","size":"normal"},{"kind":"text","at":[3.14,-2.1],"text":"Two waves overlap","size":"small"}]},{"op":"figure","id":"destruct","region":"right","frame":{"x":[0,6.28],"y":[-2.5,2.9],"axes":"edge","x_label":"position x","y_label":"displacement"},"marks":[{"kind":"fn","id":"wave_c","y":"sin(x)","domain":[0,6.28]},{"kind":"fn","id":"wave_d","y":"-sin(x)","domain":[0,6.28],"stroke":"dashed"},{"kind":"text","at":[3.14,2.5],"text":"Opposite phase","size":"normal"}]}],"checkpoint":null}}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"9c95f2d5-156e-44aa-bf4f-f983678c64e4","step":{"id":"s2","script":"Aligned crests add, and aligned troughs add. The resultant has twice the amplitude: this is constructive interference.","ops":[{"op":"figure","id":"add_left","on":"construct","marks":[{"kind":"fn","id":"sum_left","y":"2*sin(x)","domain":[0,6.28],"label":"resultant"},{"kind":"point","id":"crest_a","at":{"on":"wave_a","x":1.5708}},{"kind":"point","id":"crest_sum","at":{"on":"sum_left","x":1.5708}},{"kind":"measure","from":[1.5708,0],"to":{"at":"crest_sum"},"label":"2A"}]},{"op":"equation","id":"construct_eq","anchor":{"el":"construct","side":"below","gap":0.04},"latex":"y=y_1+y_2=A\\sin(kx)+A\\sin(kx)=2A\\sin(kx)"}],"checkpoint":null}}
{"type":"lesson.warning","request_id":"9c95f2d5-156e-44aa-bf4f-f983678c64e4","code":"step_repaired","step_hint":"s3"}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"9c95f2d5-156e-44aa-bf4f-f983678c64e4","step":{"id":"s3","script":"Opposite displacements cancel point by point. Equal amplitudes and opposite phase give complete destructive interference; unequal amplitudes would leave a nonzero resultant.","ops":[{"op":"figure","id":"add_right","on":"destruct","marks":[{"kind":"fn","id":"sum_right","y":"0","domain":[0,6.28],"label":"resultant"},{"kind":"point","id":"crest_c","at":{"on":"wave_c","x":1.5708}},{"kind":"point","id":"trough_d","at":{"on":"wave_d","x":1.5708}},{"kind":"segment","from":{"on":"wave_c","x":1.5708},"to":{"on":"wave_d","x":1.5708},"stroke":"dashed"},{"kind":"point","at":[1.5708,0],"label":"0"}]},{"op":"equation","id":"destruct_eq","anchor":{"el":"destruct","side":"below","gap":0.04},"latex":"y=y_1+y_2=A\\sin(kx)-A\\sin(kx)=0"}],"checkpoint":null}}
